98886, 50497659, 50497740, 50498319, 50498207, 50497516], "score": 64, "time": 1794662443, "title": "Advancing science and engineering with Antigravity's /teamwork", "type": "story", "url": "https://research.google/blog/advancing-science-engineering-with-antigravitys-teamwork-feature/"}, {"by": "snipedbywifi", "descendants": 12, "id": 50497132, "kids": [50498890, 50497787, 50498153, 50498016, 50498357, 50498192], "score": 72, "text": "Hey HN readers!<p>I&#x27;m snipedbywifi (<a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;gitlab.com&#x2F;snipedbywifi\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;gitlab.com&#x2F;snipedbywifi</a>), and i&#x27;ve been working on terminactory. Please try it out if you&#x27;d like to play a cozy factory game while waiting for long agent tasks to finish!<p>The game is a factory game (overused niche, i know xD), but runs in your terminal. Reason i built it? glad you asked: So basically, it started off with me wanting a terminal-native factory game. Me and the modern 5.5 claude models made a base for the game that I liked, and then i went ham adding features &#x2F; fixing some minor flaws (like adding claude code hooks so you recieve &quot;telegrams&quot; [the agent&#x27;s responses], so you can review progress directly in-game). (yes, I had heavy AI assistance, disclaimer!!!)<p>Right now, the game has basic factory features you&#x27;d expect from a game like this (build stuff, delete stuff, measure how much you&#x27;re earning, basic selection tools), along with a few more.. &quot;unexpected&quot; features. This includes a fake in-game browser that has a wiki, fake forums, some fun bits of lore, some more lore, a LOT more lore, and a research graph that shows how many items or how much RP (research points) you&#x27;d need to unlock something, and some more QOL features.<p>If anyone actually has this issue &#x2F; want of a terminal-based game that runs alongside your agents so you don&#x27;t doomscroll, do you have any suggestions, or additional ideas I could add?<p>It&#x27;s hosted on GitLab, soo, that&#x27;s one additional thing i&#x27;d like to mention<p>Thanks for reading!! snipedbywifi<p>(p.s. first HN post lol)\n(p.s. p.s. there&#x27;s a lot of hidden lore in the game, so.. lore-divers? you might like it?)", "time": 1794665154, "title": "Show HN: A terminal-native idle factory game, written in Rust with ratatui", "type": "story", "url": "https://gitlab.com/snipedbywifi/terminactory"}, {"by": "DeepLogin", "descendants": 64, "id": 50441444, "kids": [50498551, 50496902, 50498641, 50497531, 50498685, 50497505, 50496999, 50497622, 50497064, 50496980, 50497286, 50497593, 50498095, 50497430, 50497410, 50497488, 50496955, 50497922, 50497464, 50497634, 50497943, 50497619], "score": 93, "time": 1794323248, "title": "Generative AI uses more energy on non-English text", "type": "story", "url": "https://news.umich.edu/generative-ai-uses-more-energy-on-non-english-text/"}, {"by": "fursoy", "descendants": 7, "id": 50497137, "kids": [50498482, 50498636, 50497140, 50497986], "score": 28, "time": 1794665194, "title": "Show HN: Fursoy – Out-of-order RV64IMAFDV core in SystemVerilog (Linux 6.6)", "type": "story", "url": "https://github.com/FURSOY/fursoy-cpu"}, {"by": "paul_nameless", "descendants": 12, "id": 50497147, "kids": [50497919, 50498296, 50497682, 50497956, 50497173, 50497457], "score": 46, "time": 1794665292, "title": "Show HN: Agweb – a browser for agents that stays out of your way", "type": "story", "url": "https://github.com/paul-nameless/agweb"}, {"by": "cobychapple", "descendants": 62, "id": 50493062, "kids": [50494080, 50498876, 50493523, 50493873, 50493787, 50495953, 50494350, 50496782, 50494332, 50494864, 50494985, 50494309, 50495812, 50496427, 50493892, 50493697, 50494448], "score": 376, "time": 1794623309, "title": "Ggml v1.0.0", "type": "story", "url": "https://github.com/ggml-org/ggml/releases/tag/v1.0.0"}, {"by": "torutofu", "descendants": 20, "id": 50467278, "kids": [50497814, 50497586, 50498745, 50497752, 50498152, 504